  "comparisonDesign": {
    "comment": [
      "**The three requirements, and the one dimension that cannot be held constant for a closed product.**",
      "",
      "**1. Run every competitor's own harness in CI and compare with ours.** **Possible for a tool we can execute** -",
      "**which is why `open-code-review` matters: it is Apache-2.0, it runs locally, and it is a direct competitor.**",
      "**Impossible for a closed SaaS**, because **there is no API through which to point Greptile at a corpus** -",
      "**its reviews exist only where Martian captured them.**",
      "",
      "**2. The judge and the embedder must be ours.** **The judge can be, for every cell**: a shipped review is text,",
      "**and text can be re-judged.** **The embedder cannot be, for a shipped review**: it was produced by their pipeline,",
      "**and re-producing it is the same impossibility as (1).**",
      "",
      "**3. Every tool must be scored on its own corpus, ours, and every other's.** **The cross-product's holes are fixed",
      "by where each tool's outputs were captured**, so **the matrix records which cells can exist rather than pretending",
      "the grid is complete.**"
    ],
    "requirements": {
      "selfRunEveryHarness": {
        "possible": "**for any competitor that ships a local client** - which is more than the first two versions of this block allowed",
        "runnableAndModelIsOurs": [
          "agentix-e",
          "open-code-review",
          "PR-Agent (Qodo)",
          "Kodus",
          "Augment (Auggie)"
        ],
        "runnableWithAConstrainedModel": ["cubic", "Greptile (cli-review)"],
        "stillBlocked": "a reviewer whose only interface is a webhook, **which after this correction is a short list rather than a category**"
      },
      "ourJudgeAndEmbedder": {
        "judge": "ours for every cell - a shipped review is text and text can be re-judged",
        "embedder": "ours only where we run the tool; frozen where the tool ran itself"
      },
      "fullCrossProduct": {
        "whatIsComputable": "for each corpus, the tools whose outputs exist on it",
        "whatIsNot": "a corpus a closed tool was never pointed at"
      }
    },
    "corpora": {
      "martian-offline": {
        "size": "50 PRs \u00b7 173 golden comments",
        "license": "MIT, dataset and shipped reviews public",
        "hosts": "all 49 shipped tools, ours, and open-code-review",
        "why": "it is the only corpus where the field's own outputs are published"
      },
      "aacr-bench": {
        "size": "200 PRs \u00b7 1,505 expert-confirmed issues \u00b7 10 languages",
        "license": "Apache-2.0, goldens public, diffs fetched by URL",
        "hosts": "ours and open-code-review - the two tools that can be executed",
        "why": "its ground truth carries Repo Level issues, which are cross-file by construction"
      },
      "ours-real-ground-truth": {
        "size": "100 issues \u00b7 246 bug ranges",
        "license": "ours",
        "hosts": "ours, and any tool we can execute",
        "why": "the only corpus whose ground truth this project controls end to end"
      }
    },
    "knownHoles": [
      "a closed tool cannot be scored on aacr-bench, because no API exists to point it at that corpus",
      "a closed tool cannot be scored on our corpus, for the same reason",
      "the embedder dimension is frozen for every shipped review, and no amount of engineering changes that"
    ]
  },
  "toolRunnability": {
    "comment": [
      "**Which competitors this repository can execute - and the criterion is not openness.**",
      "",
      "**This block has been wrong twice, and the second correction is larger than the first.**",
      "",
      "**First version**: `open-code-review` was runnable *because it is Apache-2.0*, which made **the licence look",
      "like the gate.** **Wrong**: the test is *is the reviewer a program we possess* and *does it accept our model*.",
      "",
      "**Second version**, after the first correction: **`Greptile`, `cubic` and `Augment` were filed as",
      "`serviceOnly`** - *no program to run*. **Also wrong, and the error was the same one twice**: **a hosted product",
      "is not the same thing as a client that runs locally, and I judged three tools by the shape of their business.**",
      "",
      "**What is actually true, from their own documentation**:",
      "  **cubic** ships a CLI - `cubic review --json`, a personal API key for CI, and `cubic auth connect codex|claude-code`",
      "  **Greptile** ships `cli-review`, which runs a review **from a local checkout**, and its Enterprise tier",
      "    self-hosts **with your own models**",
      "  **Augment** ships `Auggie` - `auggie --print` is documented as *\"great for CI\"*, its custom commands include",
      "    `/code-review`, it has an official `review-pr` action, and **its pricing page lists `Model-agnostic (BYO key)`**"
    ],
    "criterion": {
      "question1": "is the reviewer a program we can possess and run ourselves?",
      "question2": "does it accept our model (or an endpoint we choose)?",
      "notTheCriterion": "whether the source is published, **and not whether the vendor's hosted product is a service** - **a hosted product with a local client is runnable, and that is the distinction the first two versions both missed**"
    },
    "tiers": {
      "runnableAndModelIsOurs": {
        "note": "**both questions answered yes, and the model can be the one this repository uses** - **five of these are observed invocable in CI, see `provenInCi`**",
        "tools": {
          "agentix-e": {
            "how": "this repository",
            "license": "ours"
          },
          "open-code-review": {
            "how": "npm i -g @alibaba-group/open-code-review, then `ocr`",
            "license": "Apache-2.0"
          },
          "PR-Agent (Qodo)": {
            "how": "pip or docker, `.pr_agent.toml`",
            "why": "**its model layer is LiteLLM**, so DeepSeek is a configuration line",
            "evidence": "**the project publishes its own benchmark - 60.1% F1 over 580 real-world issues**"
          },
          "Kodus": {
            "how": "self-hosted or docker",
            "why": "**bring-your-own-key with zero markup, across any OpenAI-compatible endpoint**"
          },
          "Augment (Auggie)": {
            "how": "npm i -g @augmentcode/auggie, then `auggie --print`",
            "why": "**its pricing page lists `Model-agnostic (BYO key)`**, and **its documentation calls `--print` *\"great for CI\"***",
            "evidence": "**an official `augmentcode/review-pr` action, and the company open-sourced its SWE-bench agent at 65.4% on SWE-bench Verified**"
          }
        }
      },
      "runnableWithAConstrainedModel": {
        "note": "**the program runs - and `cubic` and `Greptile` are both observed invocable in CI - while the model menu does not include ours**",
        "tools": {
          "cubic": {
            "how": "`curl -fsSL https://cubic.dev/install | bash` or `npx @cubic-dev-ai/cli install -g`, then `cubic review --json`",
